      "value": "@{60c0e22718009c104862d5bc|full_name}: I honestly don't remember, I just recall switching it to forced instead of dynamic and the game crashing. This was a while ago, and there are a billion things that could influence that. (Graphics driver versions, specific hardware combination, VRC build version, specific shaders in the world, etc.)\n\nI went on today to test a few different worlds with the different near clipping plane options and I found a pretty bad issue.\n\nWhen setting the near clip to forced or dynamic in this world:\n\nwrld_eda481aa-5858-4ed2-b530-3eae47c9516b\n\nthe menu becomes unusable, I can barely navigate to the rejoin instance button which undoes the forced near clip. If I set it to dynamic I need to go to my home world to change the setting.\n\nIf this was my home world and I set it to dynamic there would be no way for me to change it back without restarting the game. If the option was persistent I would be screwed. VRC could add some sort of contingency for this, but imo it's understandable that they'd rather not have it happen in the first place.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
